<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luis Vicente de Velasco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1711">1711</a>–<a href="/years/1762">1762</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Luis Vicente de Velasco e Isla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luis Vicente de Velasco was a Spanish naval officer who commanded the defence of the Morro Castle at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havana">Havana</a> during the British siege of 1762. He held out for weeks and was mortally wounded when the British stormed the fortress at the end of July. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> honoured his memory, and its navy has since kept a ship named after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luis-vicente-de-velasco.jpg" alt="Luis Vicente de Velasco" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Nicolás de la Escalera · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luis_Vicente_de_Velasco.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
